# What `vercel --prod` does NOT upload.
#
# The CLI reads only this file plus its own built-in list (`.git`, `.vercel`,
# `node_modules`, `.env.local`, ...); it never consults `.gitignore`. So the
# gitignored build output has to be named here too — the live shop must be
# built from the published sources, not from whatever `dist/` a laptop had
# lying around. The build needs none of what follows: the static site and the
# function come out of `pnpm run build` over `apps/`, `packages/` and `api/`.

# Build output and caches — regenerated by `buildCommand`
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# Documentation, specs, tests and their output
context/
docs/
apps/web/e2e/
apps/api/test/
**/test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/
.playwright-mcp/

# Agent tooling
.awos/
.claude/
.mcp.json

# Environment files never leave the laptop; the documented example is code.
.env*
!.env.example
